# project

- label: runtime is Bun
  command: grep -q 'lockfileVersion' bun.lock
- label: TUI dashboard for skill usage stats across AI coding tools
  command: grep -q 'skill usage stats' package.json
- label: written in TypeScript with strict mode enabled
  command: grep -q '"strict": true' tsconfig.json
- label: ES module project (type: module)
  command: grep -q '"type": "module"' package.json
- label: uses @opentui/core for TUI rendering
  command: grep -q '@opentui/core' package.json
- label: entry point is src/main.ts, exposed as 'skilled' bin command
  command: test -f src/main.ts && grep -q '"skilled"' package.json
- label: no build step — runs directly via bun (noEmit: true in tsconfig)
  command: grep -q '"noEmit": true' tsconfig.json
- label: unit tests cover the Grok provider
  command: bun test src/providers/grok.test.ts
- label: only runtime dependency is @opentui/core
  command: jq -e '.dependencies | keys == ["@opentui/core"]' package.json >/dev/null

# architecture
- label: provider pattern: providers implement Provider interface (name, available, collect)
  command: grep -q 'interface Provider' src/providers/base.ts
- label: five providers: ClaudeCode, Codex, Droid, OpenCode, Grok
  command: grep -q 'ClaudeCodeProvider' src/providers/claude-code.ts && grep -q 'CodexProvider' src/providers/codex.ts && grep -q 'DroidProvider' src/providers/droid.ts && grep -q 'OpenCodeProvider' src/providers/opencode.ts && grep -q 'GrokProvider' src/providers/grok.ts
- label: app.ts run() accepts Provider[] and renders the full TUI
  command: grep -q 'providers: Provider\[\]' src/app.ts
- data flow: Provider.collect() → aggregation (data.ts) → TUI (app.ts)

# data
- label: two core types: SkillCall, SkillCount (defined in models.ts)
  command: grep -q 'SkillCall' src/models.ts && grep -q 'SkillCount' src/models.ts
- label: SkillCall captures: skill, timestamp, project, sessionId, source
  command: grep -q 'sessionId' src/models.ts && grep -q 'source: string' src/models.ts
- label: aggregation functions: skillCounts, hourlyCounts, skillDetail, auditSkills (data.ts)
  command: grep -q 'export function skillCounts' src/data.ts && grep -q 'export function hourlyCounts' src/data.ts && grep -q 'export function skillDetail' src/data.ts

# provider

## claude-code
- label: skill names extracted from display field via regex /^\/([a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_-]*)(?:\s|$)/
  command: grep -q 'a-zA-Z.*a-zA-Z0-9_' src/providers/claude-code.ts
- label: builtin commands (clear, model, usage, help, etc.) are filtered out
  command: grep -q 'BUILTINS' src/providers/claude-code.ts
- label: malformed JSON lines in history are silently skipped
  command: grep -q 'catch' src/providers/claude-code.ts

## grok
- label: Grok counts a read_file of a path matching skills/<name>/SKILL.md as a skill invocation
  command: bun test src/providers/grok.test.ts -t 'counts a read_file of skills'
  tags: [grok, implemented]
- label: Grok skill name for a SKILL.md load is the directory containing the file
  command: bun test src/providers/grok.test.ts -t 'directory containing the file'
  tags: [grok, implemented]
- label: Grok ignores tool_call_update events when counting SKILL.md loads so they do not duplicate tool_call
  command: bun test src/providers/grok.test.ts -t 'ignores tool_call_update'
  tags: [grok, implemented]
- label: Grok counts a SKILL.md load at most once per session even if the file is re-read or loaded from both project and global copies
  command: bun test src/providers/grok.test.ts -t 'at most once per session'
  tags: [grok, implemented]
- label: Grok still counts slash-command invocations from <command-name> tags in user messages
  command: bun test src/providers/grok.test.ts -t 'slash-command invocations'
  tags: [grok, implemented]
- label: Grok builtin slash commands are not counted as skills when loaded via SKILL.md
  command: bun test src/providers/grok.test.ts -t 'builtin slash commands loaded via SKILL.md'
  tags: [grok, implemented]

# ui
- full-screen TUI: header, stats row, left/right panels, footer
- label: header renders animated Perlin noise background with blocky pixel font
  command: grep -q 'fbm' src/app.ts && grep -q 'PIXEL_FONT' src/app.ts
- label: stats cards show: CALLS, SKILLS, PROJECTS, SOURCES
  command: grep -q 'CALLS' src/app.ts && grep -q 'SKILLS' src/app.ts && grep -q 'PROJECTS' src/app.ts && grep -q 'SOURCES' src/app.ts
- left panel: skill frequency bar chart with animated staggered bars
- label: right panel: 16-week activity heatmap, time-of-day histogram, recent activity log
  command: grep -q 'WEEKS.*=.*16' src/app.ts && grep -q 'time of day' src/app.ts
- label: staggered animations on bars, sparkline, and heatmap cells
  command: grep -q 'barStagger' src/app.ts && grep -q 'outBack' src/app.ts
- label: Perlin noise implementation with fractional Brownian motion (fbm) in noise.ts
  command: grep -q 'export function fbm' src/noise.ts

## interaction
- label: three sort modes: by count, alphabetical, recent (cycled with 's')
  command: grep -q 'count.*alpha.*recent\|sortMode' src/app.ts
- keyboard: q quit, esc close/quit, s sort, tab direction, j/k scroll, g/G top/bottom, ctrl+d/u page, enter detail, a audit, / or f filter, r refresh

## theme
- label: GitHub-inspired dark mode theme with 14-color bar palette and 5-level green heatmap
  command: test -f src/theme.ts

# ui > interaction
- tab key toggles sort direction between ascending and descending @implemented
- bar chart bottom title shows ▲/▼ indicator next to sort mode label @implemented

# ui > analytics
- enter key on bar chart opens skill detail panel replacing right column @implemented
- skill detail panel shows per-project usage breakdown, session count, first/last used dates, and weekly usage sparkline @implemented
- 'a' key toggles audit view replacing main layout with library health insights @implemented
- audit view shows: stale skills (unused 28+ days), one-off skills (used once), declining skills (usage dropped 50%+ over last 4 weeks vs prior 4) @implemented

# desktop

## data
- label: Desktop shell is Tauri v2; the index crate is linked in-process as a library (no bundled Bun runtime, no second parser)
  id: desktop-tauri
  command: grep -q '^\[lib\]' index/Cargo.toml && grep -q 'skilled-index' desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml && grep -q '"tauri"' desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml && ! grep -rq 'bun build --compile' desktop/package.json desktop/scripts
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop indexes through skilled_index::providers::all_providers and writes the same ~/.skilled/index.db the TUI reads (custom --db path supported via settings)
  id: desktop-index-path
  command: grep -q 'all_providers' desktop/src-tauri/src/*.rs && grep -q 'write_index' desktop/src-tauri/src/*.rs && grep -q 'index.db' desktop/src-tauri/src/*.rs
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop reuses a fresh index (same 60s staleness rule as ensureIndex) instead of re-parsing on every launch
  id: desktop-index-fresh
  command: cargo test --manifest-path index/Cargo.toml --quiet read_index 2>&1 | grep -q 'test result: ok'
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop falls back to the TypeScript providers by running the installed skilled CLI with --no-index --json when the Rust index is disabled or fails, and reports which reader is active
  id: desktop-fallback
  command: grep -q -- '--no-index' desktop/src-tauri/src/*.rs && grep -q 'reader' desktop/ui/*.tsx
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Rust index records the source file of each call (file column) so the desktop can reveal the session that produced it; TUI index reader is unaffected
  id: desktop-call-file
  command: grep -q 'pub file' index/src/model.rs && grep -q 'file TEXT' index/src/db.rs && bun test src/providers/grok.test.ts >/dev/null 2>&1
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Rust providers accept per-provider path overrides and default to the current auto-detected locations
  id: desktop-path-overrides
  command: grep -q 'ProviderPaths' index/src/providers/mod.rs && cargo test --manifest-path index/Cargo.toml --quiet 2>&1 | grep -q 'test result: ok'
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop makes no network requests: CSP connect-src is none and the app has no http plugin or remote URLs
  id: desktop-offline
  command: grep -q "connect-src 'none'" desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json && ! grep -q 'tauri-plugin-http' desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml
  tags: [desktop, spec]

## parity
- label: TUI filter syntax, sort modes, sort-direction defaults and 16-week heatmap grid live in src/view.ts and are shared by the TUI and the desktop
  id: desktop-shared-view
  command: grep -q 'from "./view.js"' src/app.ts && grep -rq 'src/view' desktop/ui && bun test src/view.test.ts >/dev/null 2>&1
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop dashboard shows CALLS, SKILLS, PROJECTS, SOURCES stat cards, ranked skill bars, 16-week heatmap, hourly histogram and recent activity feed
  id: desktop-dashboard
  command: grep -q 'Heatmap' desktop/ui/views/Dashboard.tsx && grep -q 'Hourly' desktop/ui/views/Dashboard.tsx && grep -q 'Recent' desktop/ui/views/Dashboard.tsx
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop ranking supports count, alphabetical and recent sorts with a direction toggle (s and Tab keys, same as the TUI)
  id: desktop-sorts
  command: cd desktop && bun test tests/unit -t 'sort' 2>&1 | grep -q ' 0 fail'
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop filter bar accepts the TUI expression syntax (source:/s:, project:/p:, free text = skill name) and also offers source and project pickers
  id: desktop-filter
  command: cd desktop && bun test tests/unit -t 'filter' 2>&1 | grep -q ' 0 fail'
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop skill detail shows per-project breakdown, session count, first/last used and the 16-week weekly sparkline from skillDetail()
  id: desktop-detail
  command: grep -q 'skillDetail' desktop/ui/views/Detail.tsx && grep -q 'weeklyUsage' desktop/ui/views/Detail.tsx
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop audit view renders all seven auditSkills() sections (most used, rising, declining, stale, cross-project, one-off, single-project)
  id: desktop-audit
  command: for k in mostUsed rising declining stale crossProject oneOff singleProject; do grep -q "$k" desktop/ui/views/Audit.tsx || exit 1; done
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop activity view lists raw calls (skilled calls parity) with skill, time, project, session and source columns
  id: desktop-activity
  command: grep -q 'sessionId' desktop/ui/views/Activity.tsx
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop refreshes without restart: provider directories are watched with notify and a configurable interval refresh runs in the UI
  id: desktop-live
  command: grep -q 'notify' desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml && grep -q 'refreshInterval' desktop/ui/*.tsx desktop/ui/*.ts
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Aggregating a 50k-call history (counts, hourly, heatmap, audit) completes under 500ms so the UI does not freeze
  id: desktop-perf
  command: cd desktop && bun test tests/unit -t '50k' 2>&1 | grep -q ' 0 fail'
  tags: [desktop, spec]

## native
- label: Desktop restores window position and size across launches via tauri-plugin-window-state
  id: desktop-window-state
  command: grep -q 'tauri-plugin-window-state' desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop has a system tray whose tooltip and menu show live call/skill counts with Show, Refresh and Quit actions
  id: desktop-tray
  command: grep -q 'TrayIconBuilder' desktop/src-tauri/src/*.rs && grep -q 'set_tooltip' desktop/src-tauri/src/*.rs
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop keyboard shortcuts mirror the TUI (s, Tab, j/k, g/G, ctrl-d/u, Enter, a, / or f, r, Esc, q) plus Ctrl/Cmd+1-5 for views
  id: desktop-keys
  command: cd desktop && bun test tests/unit -t 'keymap' 2>&1 | grep -q ' 0 fail'
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Desktop follows the OS light/dark appearance by default with a manual override in settings
  id: desktop-theme
  command: grep -q 'prefers-color-scheme' desktop/ui/app.css && grep -q 'theme' desktop/ui/views/Settings.tsx
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: A call can be opened in the default app or revealed in the file manager via tauri-plugin-opener
  id: desktop-open-source
  command: grep -q 'tauri-plugin-opener' desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml && grep -q 'revealItemInDir' desktop/ui/*.ts desktop/ui/*.tsx desktop/ui/views/*.tsx
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Every view (skills, calls, detail, audit, providers) can be exported as JSON or CSV through a native save dialog
  id: desktop-export
  command: cd desktop && bun test tests/unit -t 'csv' 2>&1 | grep -q ' 0 fail' && grep -q 'tauri-plugin-dialog' src-tauri/Cargo.toml
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Providers view shows detection status, paths read, call count, last indexed time and which reader (Rust index or TS fallback) is active
  id: desktop-providers-view
  command: grep -q 'indexedAt' desktop/ui/views/Providers.tsx && grep -q 'paths' desktop/ui/views/Providers.tsx
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: Settings view offers per-provider path overrides, refresh interval, noise filters (skill/project patterns to hide), index DB path, reader mode, theme and tray behavior, persisted in the app config dir
  id: desktop-settings
  command: grep -q 'noise' desktop/ui/views/Settings.tsx && grep -q 'refreshInterval' desktop/ui/views/Settings.tsx && grep -q 'app_config_dir' desktop/src-tauri/src/*.rs
  tags: [desktop, spec]

## quality
- label: Desktop unit tests cover the data adapter and view models
  id: desktop-unit
  command: cd desktop && bun test tests/unit 2>&1 | grep -q ' 0 fail'
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: An end-to-end test launches the built app against a fixture history and asserts the dashboard renders fixture skills
  id: desktop-e2e
  command: test -f desktop/tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts && test -d desktop/tests/fixtures/home
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: CI builds the desktop app on Linux, macOS and Windows
  id: desktop-ci
  command: grep -q 'ubuntu' .github/workflows/desktop.yml && grep -q 'macos' .github/workflows/desktop.yml && grep -q 'windows' .github/workflows/desktop.yml
  tags: [desktop, spec]
- label: README has a Desktop section with install, dev run, build and an architecture diagram; screenshots of every view live in desktop/docs
  id: desktop-docs
  command: grep -q '## Desktop' README.md && ls desktop/docs/*.png >/dev/null 2>&1
  tags: [desktop, spec]

# domain
- A SkillCall is one observed invocation of a named skill in a provider session and project
- A SkillCount aggregates SkillCalls by skill and records frequency, distinct projects, sessions, and last use
